{
  "title": "GitHub Actions Kubernetes deploys",
  "description": "Adds a deploy workflow that, on every push to main, pushes the commit's data model image to GitHub's registry once, then runs the deploy task for the GitHub environment staging and, after it, production, whose reviewers can gate it, each with its own KUBECONFIG and CUBE_ENV secrets, one deploy at a time.",
  "depends_on": [
    "kubernetes"
  ],
  "when": "use_github_actions and use_helm",
  "ops": [
    {
      "op": "modify_file",
      "path": "README.md",
      "hunks": [
        {
          "context_before": [
            "",
            "Before the first staging or production deploy, give Cube Store a bucket of its own in `deploy/<environment>.yaml`, since the volume it uses by default suits a single node, and let the cluster pull from the image's registry, with `imagePullSecrets` if it is private."
          ],
          "removed": [],
          "added": [
            "",
            "On every push to `main`, the deploy workflow builds the image once and pushes it to GitHub's registry, deploys it to the GitHub environment `staging`, then to `production`, which waits for its required reviewers when it has some. Each environment needs the secret `KUBECONFIG`, a kubeconfig for its cluster, and, unless its Secret is managed elsewhere, the secret `CUBE_ENV`, the env file of its `CUBEJS_*` variables. Re-running an earlier run of the workflow deploys its commit again."
          ],
          "context_after": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "op": "create_file",
      "path": ".github/workflows/deploy.yml",
      "content": [
        "name: Deploy",
        "",
        "# Every push to main deploys to staging, then, once the production environment's",
        "# reviewers approve, the same image to production. Re-running an earlier run",
        "# deploys its commit again, which is how a deploy is rolled back.",
        "on:",
        "  push:",
        "    branches: [main]",
        "  workflow_dispatch:",
        "",
        "permissions:",
        "  contents: read",
        "",
        "# One deploy at a time, and never one cancelled halfway.",
        "concurrency:",
        "  group: deploy",
        "  cancel-in-progress: false",
        "",
        "jobs:",
        "  image:",
        "    name: Image",
        "    runs-on: ubuntu-latest",
        "    permissions:",
        "      contents: read",
        "      packages: write",
        "    steps:",
        "      - uses: actions/checkout@v7",
        "      - uses: jdx/mise-action@v5",
        "        with:",
        "          install_args: node",
        "      - uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@v4",
        "      - uses: docker/login-action@v4",
        "        with:",
        "          registry: ghcr.io",
        "          username: ${{ github.actor }}",
        "          password: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}",
        "      # Builds for amd64 and arm64 and pushes to ghcr.io/<owner>/<repo>, unless",
        "      # an earlier commit with the same data model pushed it already.",
        "      - run: mise run image --push",
        "",
        "  staging:",
        "    name: Staging",
        "    needs: image",
        "    runs-on: ubuntu-latest",
        "    environment: staging",
        "    permissions:",
        "      contents: read",
        "      packages: read",
        "    steps:",
        "      - uses: actions/checkout@v7",
        "      - uses: jdx/mise-action@v5",
        "      - uses: docker/login-action@v4",
        "        with:",
        "          registry: ghcr.io",
        "          username: ${{ github.actor }}",
        "          password: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}",
        "      - name: Deploy",
        "        env:",
        "          KUBECONFIG_CONTENT: ${{ secrets.KUBECONFIG }}",
        "          CUBE_ENV: ${{ secrets.CUBE_ENV }}",
        "        run: |",
        "          printf '%s\\n' \"$KUBECONFIG_CONTENT\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/kubeconfig\"",
        "          export KUBECONFIG=\"$RUNNER_TEMP/kubeconfig\"",
        "          # Without CUBE_ENV, the Secret is managed outside this repository.",
        "          if [ -n \"$CUBE_ENV\" ]; then",
        "            printf '%s\\n' \"$CUBE_ENV\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/cube.env\"",
        "            export CUBE_ENV_FILE=\"$RUNNER_TEMP/cube.env\"",
        "          fi",
        "          mise run deploy staging",
        "",
        "  production:",
        "    name: Production",
        "    needs: staging",
        "    runs-on: ubuntu-latest",
        "    environment: production",
        "    permissions:",
        "      contents: read",
        "      packages: read",
        "    steps:",
        "      - uses: actions/checkout@v7",
        "      - uses: jdx/mise-action@v5",
        "      - uses: docker/login-action@v4",
        "        with:",
        "          registry: ghcr.io",
        "          username: ${{ github.actor }}",
        "          password: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}",
        "      - name: Deploy",
        "        env:",
        "          KUBECONFIG_CONTENT: ${{ secrets.KUBECONFIG }}",
        "          CUBE_ENV: ${{ secrets.CUBE_ENV }}",
        "        run: |",
        "          printf '%s\\n' \"$KUBECONFIG_CONTENT\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/kubeconfig\"",
        "          export KUBECONFIG=\"$RUNNER_TEMP/kubeconfig\"",
        "          # Without CUBE_ENV, the Secret is managed outside this repository.",
        "          if [ -n \"$CUBE_ENV\" ]; then",
        "            printf '%s\\n' \"$CUBE_ENV\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/cube.env\"",
        "            export CUBE_ENV_FILE=\"$RUNNER_TEMP/cube.env\"",
        "          fi",
        "          mise run deploy production"
      ],
      "mode": 420
    }
  ]
}
